hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to other  edition of ask Evan in today's video I'm  going to answer questions from one of my  readers Gemma who wrote in asking one of  the biggest business pitfalls that you  can make as an entrepreneur there's a  lot that you can make so I'm going to  cut a narrow it down to three that  hopefully can help you get your business  started the first one is just chasing  the money and not doing something that  you're really passionate about and this  is a pitfall that a lot of entrepreneurs  fall into they get seduced by idea of  making a lot of money think it's going  to be really easy to start whatever  business it is and it's not it's tough  entrepreneurship is tough it's not an  easy game you're going to work harder  than you've ever worked in your life  you're gonna you know sometimes wish it  you just had a full time job instead of  doing your own company but it is really  rewarding at the end when you can get  past that survival point and are able to  build a company that you can be proud of  but those companies the ones who make it  aren't the ones we just chasing the  money they do it because they really  love doing what they're doing they feel  like they can really help people they  feel like they're having an impact and  they're making money at the same time  I'm not asking to be a prophet sorry  nonprofit and just give all your money  away it's still with you to make money  but the main purpose is to add value to  help people and to do something that  you're really passionate out so that's  where I would start start around your  interests that are on something where  you feel you can add a lot of value most  entrepreneurs don't do that to just  start up for you know a whim or  something to think they can make a lot  of money number two I would say is don't  try to do it without a customer so try  to build your custom try to build your  product around the customer it's a great  way to build a business because you have  feedback from somebody who's willing to  pay you to solve their problems soul of  entrepreneurs start a business because  the think a is a great idea and they  spend a lot of money and time and that's  spinning creating whatever product of  service and then it gets launched and  nobody buys it or five people by you  know you don't get enough money coming  in to keep the business open and you  look shutting down the better way to do  it is before you start launching your  business go and start talking to  potential customers ask them what the  problems are see if you can solve it for  them and try to get them to commit to  buying before you've actually created  whatever product or service you're going  to actually create so that's a great way  to do it you have customer buying you  have money coming in from day one it may  not be exactly what you had in mind from  the beginning but it's good because  you're building around real customer  problems and not just you know the idea  that you had in your head the third  thing is trying to do it all yourself  and this is a mistake a lot of  entrepreneurs make either because they  have trouble troubles delegating or to  think they could do it all themselves  you can't do it on yourself you have to  go and get help and recognize what  you're really good at where you add the  most value to your business so then I  ask myself all the time as I'm walked  into work is what can I do today that's  gonna add the most value to my business  it's not certain things that I'm really  good at sometimes it is but it's usually  the intersection of what I'm good at and  what I'm really passionate about and  uniquely now I'm able to deliver so what  is it that you're able to add the most  value to your business and then you know  eliminate automator or delegate out  everything else with your company and  that's a process it doesn't just happen  right away with every company but try to  figure out what's so unique about you  that will make your company different  and how can you spend a lot of your time  on that really important piece and not  everything else all the crap that comes  are going into business as well so don't  try to do it all yourself start on a  small scale the first person I hired was  one hour a day save me one hour day to  go and do other stuff with my business  things that I was really good at there's  a bunch of free programs you can get  with high school interns there's lots of  different ways it's not about the  resources you have but more how  resourceful you are so don't try to do  it yourself and that will help you build  your business so those are three common  pitfalls I hope that helps answer your  question good luck as you build your  business for those watching if you guys  liked the video please  a thumbs up below it always motivates me  to want to create more of these videos  and I'd love to hear what you have to  think you know if you agree with these  pitfalls or if you have others of your  own that you want to share please leave  it in the comments below and we'll see  you on the next episode  you
 

